    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-351132",
      "knowledge_point_id": "47989094-35d2-561f-add4-f1d427cd8a20",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding a Position Vector Given a Velocity Vector",
      "problem": "The velocity $v$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nv(t)=⟨t(6t-4),\\,12{t}^{3}⟩.\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle is at the position $(20,30)$ when $t=2,$ calculate the components of the position vector of $P$ at time $t.$\n\n$r(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,\\,3{t}^{4}-18\\,⟩$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the position vector, we need to integrate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨t(6t-4),\\,12{t}^{3}⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int t(6t-4)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 12{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+{C}_{1},\\,3{t}^{4}+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $r(2)=⟨20,30⟩.$ Substituting $t=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(2) & =⟨2(2)^{3}-2(2)^{2}+{C}_{1},\\,3(2)^{4}+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨20,30⟩ & =⟨8+{C}_{1},48+{C}_{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{1}=12$ and ${C}_{2}=-18.$ Therefore, the position vector is\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+12,\\,3{t}^{4}-18⟩.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "2t^3-2t^2+12"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "2t^3-2t^2+12",
          "choices_complete": false,
          "correct_origin": "ma_successful_grade"
        }
