    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-351261",
      "knowledge_point_id": "49aa6b33-42fb-5f28-89c5-019eadcaf1a0",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Times When a Particle Is at a Certain Location Given Its Velocity Vector",
      "problem": "The velocity $v$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nv(t)=⟨2t-3,\\,3{t}^{2}-6t+2⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle is at the position $r=⟨2,\\,0⟩$ when $t=0,$ calculate the times when the particle is at the origin. Do not round the answers.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the particle is at the origin when $t=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $t=$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The particle is at the origin when its position is $r=⟨0,0⟩.$ So first, we need to compute the position function of the particle.\n\nTo compute the position vector, we need to integrate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨2t-3,\\,3{t}^{2}-6t+2⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int (2t-3)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int (3{t}^{2}-6t+2)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{2}-3t+{C}_{1},\\,{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+2t+{C}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $r(0)=⟨2,0⟩.$ Substituting $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨0-0+{C}_{1},\\,0-0+0+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨2,0⟩ & =⟨{C}_{1},\\,{C}_{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{1}=2$ and ${C}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the position of $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨{t}^{2}-3t+2,\\,{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the times at which the particle is at the origin, we solve the equation $r(t)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{t}^{2}-3t+2,\\,{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+2t⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-3t+2 & =(t-1)(t-2)=0\\,⇒\\,t=1,2, \\\\ {t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+2t & =t(t-1)(t-2)=0\\,⇒\\,t=0,1,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values of $t$ that satisfy both equations are $t=1$ and $t=2.$ \n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the particle is at the origin when\n$t=1$ and $t=2.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "1"
            }
