    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-347213",
      "knowledge_point_id": "49aa6b33-42fb-5f28-89c5-019eadcaf1a0",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Times When a Particle Is at a Certain Location Given Its Velocity Vector",
      "problem": "The velocity $v$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nv(t)=⟨2\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t),\\,2t-5⟩,\\,t\\in (0,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle is at the position $r=⟨0,6⟩$ when $t=0,$ find the times when the particle intersects the $x$-axis. Do not round the answers.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the particle intersects the $x$-axis when $t=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $t=$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The particle intersects the $x$-axis when its position is $r=⟨x,0⟩,$ where $x$ is arbitrary. So first, we need to compute the position function of the particle.\n\nTo compute the position vector, we need to integrate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨2\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t),\\,2t-5⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int 2\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\int (2t-5)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t)+{C}_{1},\\,{t}^{2}-5t+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $r(0)=⟨0,6⟩.$ Substituting $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+{C}_{1},\\,{0}^{2}-5(0)+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨0,6⟩ & =⟨{C}_{1},\\,{C}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we must have ${C}_{1}=0$ and ${C}_{2}=6.$ Therefore, the position of $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t),\\,{t}^{2}-5t+6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the times  when the particle intersects the $x$-axis, we solve for the times at which the $y$-coordinate of the position vector is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-5t+6 & =0 \\\\ (t-2)(t-3) & =0 \\\\ t & =2,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the particle intersects the $x$-axis when $t=2$ and $t=3.$",
      "answer_fields": [
