    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-122471",
      "knowledge_point_id": "279c5e4e-db19-584b-becb-10864fcba188",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding a Position Vector Given an Acceleration Vector",
      "problem": "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\na(t)=⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},0⟩\\,,\\,t\\in (0,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle is at the position $(2,3)$ and has velocity $⟨1,-1⟩$ when $t=1,$ calculate the position vector of $P$ at time $t.$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the position vector, we need to integrate the velocity vector. To find the velocity vector, we first need to integrate the acceleration vector. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},0⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})\\text{d}t,\\int 0\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t}+{C}_{1},{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(1)=⟨1,-1⟩.$ Substituting $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨\\frac{1}{1}+{C}_{1},{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨1,-1⟩ & =⟨1+{C}_{1},{C}_{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{1}=0$ and ${C}_{2}=-1.$ Therefore, the velocity vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =⟨\\frac{1}{t},-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the position vector by integrating the velocity vector.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨\\frac{1}{t},-1⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int (-1)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+{C}_{3},-t+{C}_{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $r(1)=⟨2,3⟩.$ Substituting $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+{C}_{3},-1+{C}_{4}⟩ \\\\ ⟨2,3⟩ & =⟨{C}_{3},-1+{C}_{4}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{3}=2$ and ${C}_{4}=4.$ Therefore, the position of $P$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,4-t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
