    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-351538",
      "knowledge_point_id": "279c5e4e-db19-584b-becb-10864fcba188",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding a Position Vector Given an Acceleration Vector",
      "problem": "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\na(t)=⟨-{e}^{-t},\\,20{t}^{3}⟩.\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle is at the position $(3,-2)$ and has velocity $⟨0,\\,1⟩$ when $t=0,$ calculate the position vector of $P$ at time $t.$\n\n$r(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,\\,{t}^{5}+t-2\\,⟩$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the position vector, we need to integrate the velocity vector. To find the velocity vector, we first need to integrate the acceleration vector. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨-{e}^{-t},\\,20{t}^{3}⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int (-{e}^{-t})\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 20{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{-t}+{C}_{1},\\,5{t}^{4}+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(0)=⟨0,1⟩.$ Substituting $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(0) & =⟨{e}^{0}+{C}_{1},\\,5(0)^{4}+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨0,1⟩ & =⟨1+{C}_{1},\\,{C}_{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso, we must have ${C}_{1}=-1$ and ${C}_{2}=1.$ Therefore, the velocity vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =⟨{e}^{-t}-1,\\,5{t}^{4}+1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the position vector by integrating the velocity vector.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨{e}^{-t}-1,\\,5{t}^{4}+1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int ({e}^{-t}-1)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int (5{t}^{4}+1)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{-t}-t+{C}_{3},\\,{t}^{5}+t+{C}_{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $r(0)=⟨3,-2⟩.$ Substituting $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨-{e}^{0}-0+{C}_{3},\\,{0}^{5}+0+{C}_{4}⟩ \\\\ ⟨3,-2⟩ & =⟨-1+{C}_{3},\\,{C}_{4}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso, we must have ${C}_{3}=4$ and ${C}_{4}=-2.$ Therefore, the position of $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨-{e}^{-t}-t+4,\\,{t}^{5}+t-2⟩.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
