    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-351517",
      "knowledge_point_id": "279c5e4e-db19-584b-becb-10864fcba188",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding a Position Vector Given an Acceleration Vector",
      "problem": "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\na(t)=⟨48(2t+1)^{2},\\,-6⟩.\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle is at the position $(2,-1)$ and has velocity $⟨8,\\,5⟩$ when $t=0,$ calculate the position vector of $P$ at time $t.$\n\n$r(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,\\,-3{t}^{2}+5t-1\\,⟩$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the position vector, we need to integrate the velocity vector. To find the velocity vector, we first need to integrate the acceleration vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨48(2t+1)^{2},\\,-6⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int 48(2t+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int (-6)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8(2t+1)^{3}+{C}_{1},\\,-6t+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(0)=⟨8,5⟩.$ Substituting $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(0) & =⟨8(1)^{3}+{C}_{1},\\,-6(0)+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨8,5⟩ & =⟨8+{C}_{1},\\,{C}_{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso, we must have ${C}_{1}=0$ and ${C}_{2}=5.$ Therefore, the velocity vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t)=⟨8(2t+1)^{3},\\,-6t+5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate the velocity vector to obtain the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨8(2t+1)^{3},\\,-6t+5⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int 8(2t+1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int (-6t+5)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(2t+1)^{4}+{C}_{3},\\,-3{t}^{2}+5t+{C}_{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $r(0)=(2,-1).$ Substituting $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨(1)^{4}+{C}_{3},\\,0+0+{C}_{4}⟩ \\\\ ⟨2,-1⟩ & =⟨1+{C}_{3},\\,{C}_{4}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso, we must have ${C}_{3}=1$ and ${C}_{4}=-1.$ Therefore, the position vector of $P$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(2t+1)^{4}+1,\\,-3{t}^{2}+5t-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
